IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgc2-common`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 6 Division 2, sections 205AA to 205AF -- resignation of an auditor, the written statement of reasons, the Court's power to stop it
-- being sent, the privilege against defamation, and the appointment of a new auditor. LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- "14 days beginning on the date on which ..." counts that date as day 1, so the last day is the date plus 13 (fork line F-P3 in NOTES.md);
-- "within 14 days after ..." counts it out, so the last day is the date plus 14 (P1 of the keel). Where the text says "within 14 days of the
-- appointment" (s 205AF(1)(d)) it is read as "after" (fork line F-P3).

§ `Sections 205AA to 205AF: the acts and parties of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `s 205AA act` IS ONE OF
    `s 205AA(3) lodge with the Registrar a notification that the company has received a notice of resignation`
    `s 205AB(2) notify the auditor and the company whether the Registrar consents to the resignation`
    `s 205AC(1) send a copy of the written statement to every member of the company`
    `s 205AC(3)(a) give notice of the application to the auditor of the company`
    `s 205AC(3)(b) give notice of the application to the company and the auditor of the company`
    `s 205AD(3) send a notice setting out the effect of the Court's directions to every member and, unless already named as a party, to the auditor`
    `s 205AD(4) give notice of the Court's decision to the auditor and send a copy of the written statement to every member and to the auditor`
    `s 205AF(1)(c) call a general meeting for the purpose of appointing an auditor in place of the auditor who resigns`
    `s 205AF(1)(d) lodge with the Registrar a notification of the appointment of the new auditor`

DECLARE `s 205AC(3) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 205AC(3)(a) the company`
    `s 205AC(3)(b) any other person who claims to be aggrieved by the written statement`

§ `Section 205AA(4): public interest company and non-public interest company`

-- "public interest company" means a company which is listed or in the process of issuing its debt or equity instruments for trading on an
-- approved exchange in Singapore, or such other company as the Minister may prescribe. A "means" definition: JUST FALSE off it.
-- src:19280 | “public interest company” means a company which is listed or in
-- src:19281 | the process of issuing its debt or equity instruments for
-- src:19282 | trading on an approved exchange in Singapore, or such other
-- src:19283 | company as the Minister may prescribe.
@ref s 205AA(4) "public interest company" (src:19280-19283)
GIVEN `the company is listed on an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in the process of issuing its debt or equity instruments for trading on an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has prescribed the company as a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AA(4) "public interest company" the company is a public interest company` MEANS
    IF `the company is listed on an approved exchange in Singapore` OR `the company is in the process of issuing its debt or equity instruments for trading on an approved exchange in Singapore` OR `the Minister has prescribed the company as a public interest company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'public interest company' means a company which is listed or in the process of issuing its debt or equity instruments for trading on an approved exchange in Singapore, or such other company as the Minister may prescribe" (a "means" definition)

-- src:19275 | (4) In this section and sections 205AB, 205AC and 205AF —
-- src:19277 | “non‑public interest company” means a company other than a
-- src:19278 | public interest company;
@ref s 205AA(4) "non-public interest company" (src:19275-19278)
GIVEN `the company is a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AA(4) "non-public interest company" the company is a non-public interest company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public interest company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'non-public interest company' means a company other than a public interest company" (a "means" definition)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 205AA(1) to (3): resignation of the auditor of a non-public interest company`

-- "(other than a company which is a subsidiary company of a public interest company)": one of the six questions decided site by site
-- (Guide ruling of 2026-11-05): the carve-out is answered NOTHING, because section 205AB, not this section, governs the excluded company (fork line F-X1).
-- src:19245 | 205AA.—(1) An auditor of a non‑public interest company (other
-- src:19246 | than a company which is a subsidiary company of a public interest
-- src:19247 | company) may resign before the end of the term of office for which
-- src:19248 | the auditor was appointed by giving the company a notice of
-- src:19249 | resignation in writing.
@ref s 205AA(1) (src:19245-19249)
GIVEN `the company is a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a subsidiary company of a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given before the end of the term of office for which the auditor was appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AA(1) the auditor may resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public interest company` OR `the company is a subsidiary company of a public interest company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a non-public interest company (other than a company which is a subsidiary company of a public interest company) may resign" gives this power to no other auditor; section 205AB deals with them (fork line F-X1)
    ELSE (IF `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing` AND `the notice is given before the end of the term of office for which the auditor was appointed`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to resign "before the end of the term of office ... by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing"; the subsection does not say a resignation otherwise given is barred (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

-- (2): the term of office expires at the end of the day on which notice is given, or, if the notice specifies a time on a later day, at that time.
-- The answer is the day on which the term of office expires.
-- src:19253 | (2) Where a notice of resignation is given under subsection (1), the
-- src:19254 | auditor’s term of office expires —
-- src:19256 | (a) at the end of the day on which notice is given to the
-- src:19257 | company; or
-- src:19259 | (b) if the notice specifies a time on a later day for the purpose,
-- src:19260 | at that time.
@ref s 205AA(2) (src:19253-19260)
GIVEN `the day the notice of resignation is given to the company` IS A DATE
      `the notice specifies a time on a later day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later day the notice specifies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205AA(2) the day on which the auditor's term of office expires` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies a time on a later day` AND `the later day the notice specifies` GREATER THAN `the day the notice of resignation is given to the company`
    THEN `the later day the notice specifies`
    ELSE `the day the notice of resignation is given to the company`

-- (3): "Within 14 days beginning on the date on which a company receives a notice of resignation ... the company must lodge with the Registrar a notification of that fact".
-- src:19264 | (3) Within 14 days beginning on the date on which a company
-- src:19265 | receives a notice of resignation under subsection (1), the company
-- src:19270 | must lodge with the Registrar a notification of that fact in such form
-- src:19271 | as the Registrar may require.
@ref s 205AA(3) (src:19264-19271)
GIVEN `the date the company receives the notice of resignation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205AA(3) the last day for the company to lodge the notification` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company receives the notice of resignation` 13 Days

@ref s 205AA(3) (src:19264-19271)
GIVEN `the date the company receives the notice of resignation` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged the notification with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company lodged the notification` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AA(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the notification` MEANS
    IF `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
          `the company has lodged the notification with the Registrar`
          `the day the company lodged the notification`
          (`s 205AA(3) the last day for the company to lodge the notification` `the date the company receives the notice of resignation`)
          `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 14 days beginning on the date on which a company receives a notice of resignation under subsection (1), the company must lodge with the Registrar a notification of that fact" (a duty met in time, or not yet due: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 205AA(3) (src:19264-19271)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the date the company receives the notice of resignation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
`s 205AA(3) the company must lodge the notification with the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205AA(3) lodge with the Registrar a notification that the company has received a notice of resignation`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the date the company receives the notice of resignation` (`s 205AA(3) the last day for the company to lodge the notification` `the date the company receives the notice of resignation`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge with the Registrar a notification of the notice of resignation within 14 days beginning on the date it received the notice"

§ `Section 205AB: resignation of the auditor of a public interest company, or a subsidiary of one`

-- (1): an auditor of a public interest company, or a subsidiary company of one, may resign by written notice if (a) the auditor applied to the Registrar for consent,
-- gave a written statement of reasons, and at or about the same time told the company in writing and gave it the statement; and (b) the Registrar has consented.
-- "if" with no "only": a "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1).
-- src:19290 | 205AB.—(1) An auditor of a public interest company, or a
-- src:19291 | subsidiary company of a public interest company, may by giving
-- src:19292 | the company a notice of resignation in writing, resign before the end
-- src:19293 | of the term of office for which the auditor was appointed, if —
-- src:19295 | (a) the auditor has applied for consent from the Registrar to the
-- src:19296 | resignation and provided a written statement of the
-- src:19297 | auditor’s reasons for resigning and, at or about the same
-- src:19298 | time as the application, notified the company in writing of
-- src:19299 | the application to the Registrar and provided the company
-- src:19300 | with the written statement of the auditor’s reasons for
-- src:19301 | resigning; and
-- src:19303 | (b) the consent of the Registrar has been given.
@ref s 205AB(1) (src:19290-19303)
GIVEN `the company is a public interest company or a subsidiary company of a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has applied to the Registrar for consent to the resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has provided the Registrar with a written statement of the auditor's reasons for resigning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at or about the time of the application the auditor notified the company in writing of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at or about the time of the application the auditor provided the company with the written statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has consented to the resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AB(1) the auditor may resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public interest company or a subsidiary company of a public interest company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for "an auditor of a public interest company, or a subsidiary company of a public interest company"; section 205AA deals with the others
    ELSE (IF     `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing`
             AND `the auditor has applied to the Registrar for consent to the resignation`
             AND `the auditor has provided the Registrar with a written statement of the auditor's reasons for resigning`
             AND `at or about the time of the application the auditor notified the company in writing of the application`
             AND `at or about the time of the application the auditor provided the company with the written statement`
             AND `the Registrar has consented to the resignation`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may ... resign ..., if -- (a) ...; and (b) the consent of the Registrar has been given" (a "may" whose "if" gate failed: the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

-- (2): "The Registrar must, as soon as practicable after receiving the application ..., notify the auditor and the company whether it consents".
-- A duty of an official: encoded for what it means to the person, that the auditor and the company are to be told. No number of days is stated: no breach path.
-- src:19307 | (2) The Registrar must, as soon as practicable after receiving the
-- src:19308 | application from an auditor under subsection (1), notify the auditor
-- src:19309 | and the company whether it consents to the resignation of the auditor.
@ref s 205AB(2) (src:19307-19309)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received the auditor's application under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AB(2) the auditor and the company are to be notified whether the Registrar consents` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received the auditor's application under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what the Registrar must do after receiving an application and says nothing where none has been received

@ref s 205AB(2) (src:19307-19309)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
`s 205AB(2) the Registrar must notify the auditor and the company whether it consents` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 205AB(2) notify the auditor and the company whether the Registrar consents to the resignation`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- the section says "as soon as practicable"; read as Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not notify the auditor and the company whether it consents to the resignation"

-- (3): a statement made by an auditor in the application, or in answer to the Registrar's inquiry about the reasons: (a) is not admissible in evidence in any civil or
-- criminal proceedings against the auditor; and (b) subject to (4), may not be made the ground of a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor.
DECLARE `s 205AB(3) proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `s 205AB(3) civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor`
    `s 205AB(3) a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor`
    `s 205AB(4) disciplinary proceedings commenced under the Accountants Act 2004 against the auditor`
    `s 205AB(3) any other proceedings`

-- src:19313 | (3) A statement made by an auditor in an application to the
-- src:19314 | Registrar under subsection (1)(a) or in answer to an inquiry by the
-- src:19315 | Registrar relating to the reasons for the application —
-- src:19317 | (a) is not admissible in evidence in any civil or criminal
-- src:19318 | proceedings against the auditor; and
@ref s 205AB(3)(a) (src:19313-19318)
GIVEN `the statement was made in the auditor's application under subsection (1)(a) or in answer to an inquiry by the Registrar relating to the reasons for the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      proceedings IS A `s 205AB(3) proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AB(3)(a) the statement is admissible in evidence in the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the statement was made in the auditor's application under subsection (1)(a) or in answer to an inquiry by the Registrar relating to the reasons for the application`
    THEN (CONSIDER proceedings
          WHEN `s 205AB(3) civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not admissible in evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor" (a flat negative)
          WHEN `s 205AB(3) a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not admissible in evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor" (a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor is civil or criminal proceedings)
          WHEN `s 205AB(4) disciplinary proceedings commenced under the Accountants Act 2004 against the auditor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of civil or criminal proceedings; disciplinary proceedings are for subsection (4)
          WHEN `s 205AB(3) any other proceedings` THEN NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) is about a statement made in the application or in answer to the Registrar's inquiry

-- src:19323 | (b) subject to subsection (4), may not be made the ground of a
-- src:19324 | prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor,
@ref s 205AB(3)(b) (src:19323-19324)
GIVEN `the statement was made in the auditor's application under subsection (1)(a) or in answer to an inquiry by the Registrar relating to the reasons for the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      proceedings IS A `s 205AB(3) proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AB(3)(b) the statement may be made the ground of a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor` MEANS
    IF `the statement was made in the auditor's application under subsection (1)(a) or in answer to an inquiry by the Registrar relating to the reasons for the application`
    THEN (CONSIDER proceedings
          WHEN `s 205AB(3) a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be made the ground of a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor" (a flat negative)
          WHEN `s 205AB(3) civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be made the ground of a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor" (civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor are an action, a suit or a prosecution)
          WHEN `s 205AB(4) disciplinary proceedings commenced under the Accountants Act 2004 against the auditor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection (4)", which says the statement may be used in disciplinary proceedings
          WHEN `s 205AB(3) any other proceedings` THEN NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks of a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) is about a statement made in the application or in answer to the Registrar's inquiry

-- "a certificate by the Registrar that the statement was made in the application or in the answer ... is conclusive evidence that the statement was so made".
-- src:19326 | and a certificate by the Registrar that the statement was made in the
-- src:19327 | application or in the answer to the inquiry by the Registrar is
-- src:19328 | conclusive evidence that the statement was so made.
@ref s 205AB(3) (src:19326-19328)
GIVEN `the Registrar has certified that the statement was made in the application or in the answer to the Registrar's inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AB(3) the Registrar's certificate is conclusive evidence that the statement was made in the application or the answer` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has certified that the statement was made in the application or in the answer to the Registrar's inquiry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what a certificate proves and says nothing where there is none

-- src:19332 | (4) Despite subsection (3), the statement referred to therein may be
-- src:19333 | used in any disciplinary proceedings commenced under the
-- src:19334 | Accountants Act 2004 against the auditor.
@ref s 205AB(4) (src:19332-19334)
GIVEN proceedings IS A `s 205AB(3) proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AB(4) the statement may be used in the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceedings
    WHEN `s 205AB(4) disciplinary proceedings commenced under the Accountants Act 2004 against the auditor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 205AB(3) civil or criminal proceedings against the auditor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) permits use "in any disciplinary proceedings commenced under the Accountants Act 2004 against the auditor" and speaks of no other proceedings
    WHEN `s 205AB(3) a prosecution, an action or a suit against the auditor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): as above
    WHEN `s 205AB(3) any other proceedings` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): as above

-- (5): the resignation takes effect on the last to occur of (a) the day specified in the notice (if any), (b) the day the Registrar notifies consent, (c) the day (if any) the Registrar fixes.
-- src:19338 | (5) The resignation of an auditor of a public interest company, or
-- src:19339 | subsidiary company of a public interest company, takes effect —
-- src:19341 | (a) on the day (if any) specified for the purpose in the notice of
-- src:19342 | resignation;
-- src:19344 | (b) on the day on which the Registrar notifies the auditor and
-- src:19345 | the company of the Registrar’s consent to the resignation;
-- src:19346 | or
-- src:19348 | (c) on the day (if any) fixed by the Registrar for the purpose,
-- src:19350 | whichever last occurs.
@ref s 205AB(5) (src:19338-19350)
GIVEN `the notice of resignation specifies a day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice of resignation specifies` IS A DATE
      `the day the Registrar notifies the auditor and the company of the Registrar's consent` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has fixed a day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar has fixed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205AB(5) the day the resignation takes effect` MEANS
    LET `after (a)` MEANS (IF `the notice of resignation specifies a day` AND `the day the notice of resignation specifies` GREATER THAN `the day the Registrar notifies the auditor and the company of the Registrar's consent`
                           THEN `the day the notice of resignation specifies`
                           ELSE `the day the Registrar notifies the auditor and the company of the Registrar's consent`)
    IN IF `the Registrar has fixed a day` AND `the day the Registrar has fixed` GREATER THAN `after (a)`
       THEN `the day the Registrar has fixed`
       ELSE `after (a)`

§ `Section 205AC: the written statement is sent to the members unless the Court is asked to stop it`

-- src:19357 | 205AC.—(1) Where an auditor of a public interest company, or a
-- src:19358 | subsidiary company of a public interest company, gives the company
-- src:19359 | a notice of resignation under section 205AB, the company must
-- src:19360 | within 14 days after receiving the notice of resignation and the written
-- src:19361 | statement of the auditor’s reasons for resigning (called in this section
-- src:19362 | and sections 205AD and 205AE the written statement) send a copy of
-- src:19363 | the written statement to every member of the company.
@ref s 205AC(1) (src:19357-19363)
GIVEN `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205AC(1) the last day for the company to send a copy of the written statement to every member` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons` 14 Days

@ref s 205AC(1) (src:19357-19363)
GIVEN `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons` IS A DATE
      `the company has sent a copy of the written statement to every member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company sent the copies` IS A DATE
      `copies need not be sent out because an application has been made to the Court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AC(1) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the written statement to every member` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `copies need not be sent out because an application has been made to the Court under subsection (2)`)
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the company has sent a copy of the written statement to every member`
              `the day the company sent the copies`
              (`s 205AC(1) the last day for the company to send a copy of the written statement to every member` `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons`)
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must within 14 days after receiving the notice of resignation and the written statement ... send a copy of the written statement to every member of the company" (a duty met in time, or not yet due, or excused by subsection (2): the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 205AC(1) (src:19357-19363)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
`s 205AC(1) the company must send a copy of the written statement to every member` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205AC(1) send a copy of the written statement to every member of the company`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons` (`s 205AC(1) the last day for the company to send a copy of the written statement to every member` `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send a copy of the written statement to every member within 14 days after receiving the notice of resignation and the statement"

-- (2): copies need not be sent if an application is made to the Court within 14 days beginning on the date on which the company received the written statement,
-- by the company or any other person who claims to be aggrieved, for a determination that the auditor abused the written statement or is using it to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter.
-- "need not ... if": a relief gated by an "if"; a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1).
-- src:19367 | (2) Copies of the written statement need not be sent out if an
-- src:19368 | application is made to the Court within 14 days, beginning on the date
-- src:19369 | on which the company received the written statement, by either the
-- src:19370 | company or any other person who claims to be aggrieved by the
-- src:19371 | written statement, for a determination that the auditor has abused the
-- src:19376 | use of the written statement or is using the provisions of this section to
-- src:19377 | secure needless publicity for defamatory matter.
@ref s 205AC(2) (src:19367-19377)
GIVEN `the day the company received the written statement` IS A DATE
      `an application has been made to the Court by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved by the written statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the application is for a determination that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using the provisions of section 205AC to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AC(2) copies of the written statement need not be sent out` MEANS
    IF     `an application has been made to the Court by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved by the written statement`
       AND `the application is for a determination that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using the provisions of section 205AC to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`
       AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company received the written statement` `the day the application was made` 13 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Copies of the written statement need not be sent out if an application is made to the Court within 14 days, beginning on the date on which the company received the written statement, by either the company or any other person who claims to be aggrieved ..., for a determination that the auditor has abused ..." (an "if" gate; a failed "if" counts as the text's no: marginal reading (a), fork lines F-M1 and F-P3)

-- (3): the applicant must give notice of the application: the company, to the auditor; any other person, to the company and the auditor.
-- No time limit is stated: no breach path.
-- src:19381 | (3) In the case where an application is made under subsection (2)
-- src:19382 | by —
-- src:19384 | (a) the company — the company must give notice of the
-- src:19385 | application to the auditor of the company; or
-- src:19387 | (b) any other person — that person must give notice of the
-- src:19388 | application to the company and the auditor of the company.
@ref s 205AC(3) (src:19381-19388)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 205AC(3) applicant`
      `the applicant has given notice of the application to the auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has given notice of the application to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AC(3) the applicant is in default of the duty to give notice of the application` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 205AC(3)(a) the company` THEN (IF `the applicant has given notice of the application to the auditor of the company` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
    WHEN `s 205AC(3)(b) any other person who claims to be aggrieved by the written statement` THEN (IF `the applicant has given notice of the application to the company` AND `the applicant has given notice of the application to the auditor of the company` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 205AC(3) (src:19381-19388)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
`s 205AC(3)(a) the company that applies must give notice of the application to the auditor` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205AC(3)(a) give notice of the application to the auditor of the company`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company that applied to the Court did not give notice of the application to the auditor"

@ref s 205AC(3) (src:19381-19388)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
`s 205AC(3)(b) any other person who applies must give notice of the application to the company and the auditor` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 205AC(3)(b) give notice of the application to the company and the auditor of the company`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person who applied to the Court did not give notice of the application to the company and the auditor"

-- src:19392 | (4) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the
-- src:19393 | company and every director of the company who is in default shall
-- src:19394 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:19395 | fine not exceeding $5,000.
