      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AC(4) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 205AC(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 205(17) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) any other person` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and every director of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" names the persons it makes guilty (the offence's own question; split site (i), fork line F-E1)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1)" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)

@ref s 205AC(4) (src:19392-19395)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205AC(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 205AC(4) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 205AC(4) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with section 205AC(1)` person EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 5000
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 205AD: the Court may order the written statement not to be sent out`

-- src:19401 | 205AD.—(1) This section applies if an application has been made
-- src:19402 | under section 205AC(2) in relation to a written statement given by an
-- src:19403 | auditor.
@ref s 205AD(1) (src:19401-19403)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 205AC(2) in relation to a written statement given by an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AD(1) section 205AD applies` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made under section 205AC(2) in relation to a written statement given by an auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if an application has been made under section 205AC(2)" (an "if" gate; marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)

-- (2): if the Court is satisfied that the auditor abused the use of the statement or is using it to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter,
-- the Court (a) must direct that copies are not to be sent; and (b) may order the auditor, though not a party to the application, to pay the applicant's costs in whole or in part.
-- What this means to the person: where the Court is so satisfied, the statement is not sent (a) and the auditor may be ordered to pay costs (b).
-- src:19407 | (2) If the Court is satisfied that the auditor has abused the use of the
-- src:19408 | written statement or is using the written statement to secure needless
-- src:19409 | publicity for any defamatory matter, the Court —
-- src:19411 | (a) must direct that copies of the written statement are not to be
-- src:19412 | sent under section 205AC(1); and
-- src:19414 | (b) may order the auditor, though not a party to the application,
-- src:19415 | to pay the applicant’s costs on the application in whole or
-- src:19416 | in part.
@ref s 205AD(2) (src:19407-19416)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 205AC(2) in relation to a written statement given by an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using it to secure needless publicity for any defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AD(2)(a) the Court is required to direct that copies of the written statement are not to be sent` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made under section 205AC(2) in relation to a written statement given by an auditor` AND `the Court is satisfied that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using it to secure needless publicity for any defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Court is satisfied that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using the written statement to secure needless publicity for any defamatory matter, the Court (a) must direct that copies of the written statement are not to be sent" (an "if" gate on a duty; marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)

@ref s 205AD(2)(b) (src:19407-19416)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 205AC(2) in relation to a written statement given by an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using it to secure needless publicity for any defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AD(2)(b) the Court may order the auditor to pay the applicant's costs in whole or in part` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made under section 205AC(2) in relation to a written statement given by an auditor` AND `the Court is satisfied that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using it to secure needless publicity for any defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court's power to order costs is stated for the case where it is satisfied of the abuse (a "may" whose "if" gate failed: the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

-- (3): if the Court gives directions under (2)(a), the company must, within 14 days beginning on the date the directions are given, send a notice setting out their effect to
-- (a) every member; and (b) unless already named as a party, the auditor who gave the written statement.
-- src:19420 | (3) If the Court gives directions under subsection (2)(a), the
-- src:19421 | company must, within 14 days beginning on the date on which the
-- src:19422 | directions are given send a notice setting out the effect of the
-- src:19423 | directions to —
-- src:19425 | (a) every member of the company; and
-- src:19430 | (b) unless already named as a party to the proceedings, the
-- src:19431 | auditor who gave the written statement.
@ref s 205AD(3) (src:19420-19431)
GIVEN `the day the Court gives the directions` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205AD(3) the last day for the company to send the notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the Court gives the directions` 13 Days

@ref s 205AD(3) (src:19420-19431)
GIVEN `the day the Court gives the directions` IS A DATE
      `the company has sent the notice to every member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is already named as a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has sent the notice to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company sent the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AD(3) the company is in default of the duty to send a notice setting out the effect of the directions` MEANS
    IF `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
          (`the company has sent the notice to every member` AND (`the auditor is already named as a party to the proceedings` OR `the company has sent the notice to the auditor`))
          `the day the company sent the notice`
          (`s 205AD(3) the last day for the company to send the notice` `the day the Court gives the directions`)
          `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Court gives directions under subsection (2)(a), the company must, within 14 days beginning on the date on which the directions are given send a notice setting out the effect of the directions to (a) every member of the company; and (b) unless already named as a party to the proceedings, the auditor" (a duty met in time, or not yet due: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 205AD(3) (src:19420-19431)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the Court gives the directions` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
`s 205AD(3) the company must send a notice setting out the effect of the directions` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205AD(3) send a notice setting out the effect of the Court's directions to every member and, unless already named as a party, to the auditor`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the Court gives the directions` (`s 205AD(3) the last day for the company to send the notice` `the day the Court gives the directions`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send a notice setting out the effect of the Court's directions within 14 days beginning on the date the directions were given"

-- (4): if the Court decides not to grant the application, the company must, within 14 days beginning on the date the decision is made or the proceedings are discontinued for any reason,
-- (a) give notice of the decision to the auditor; and (b) send a copy of the written statement to every member and to that auditor.
