§ `Section 205AE: privilege against an action for defamation`

DECLARE `s 205AE publication` IS ONE OF
    `s 205AE(a) publication of the written statement to a member pursuant to section 205AC(1)`
    `s 205AE(b) publication of the written statement to a member pursuant to section 205AD(4)(b)`
    `s 205AE any other publication`

-- "A person is not liable to any action for defamation at the suit of any person (a) in the absence of malice, in respect of the publication of the written statement to the member
-- pursuant to section 205AC(1); or (b) in respect of the publication ... pursuant to section 205AD(4)(b)." Named for the protection: JUST TRUE where it is given, NOTHING where the
-- section is silent (a publication with malice under (a) is not covered by (a); the section does not say the person is liable).
-- src:19457 | 205AE. A person is not liable to any action for defamation at the
-- src:19458 | suit of any person —
-- src:19460 | (a) in the absence of malice, in respect of the publication of the
-- src:19461 | written statement to the member of the company pursuant
-- src:19462 | to section 205AC(1); or
-- src:19464 | (b) in respect of the publication of the written statement to the
-- src:19465 | member of the company pursuant to section 205AD(4)(b).
@ref s 205AE (src:19457-19465)
GIVEN publication IS A `s 205AE publication`
      `there is malice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AE the person has the privilege against an action for defamation for the publication` MEANS
    CONSIDER publication
    WHEN `s 205AE(a) publication of the written statement to a member pursuant to section 205AC(1)` THEN (IF `there is malice` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) gives the privilege "in the absence of malice" and says nothing where there is malice
    WHEN `s 205AE(b) publication of the written statement to a member pursuant to section 205AD(4)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 205AE any other publication` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section names two publications and says nothing of any other

§ `Section 205AF: appointing a new auditor in place of a resigning auditor`

-- (1)(c): the directors must call a general meeting as soon as practicable, and in any case not more than 3 months after the date of the auditor's resignation, to appoint an auditor in place.
-- "as soon as practicable" has no number and is not computed; the 3 months is the outer limit the rule checks.
-- src:19471 | 205AF.—(1) Subject to subsection (3), if —
-- src:19473 | (a) an auditor of a non‑public interest company (other than a
-- src:19474 | subsidiary company of a public interest company) gives
-- src:19475 | notice of resignation under section 205AA(1); or
-- src:19477 | (b) an auditor of a public interest company, or a subsidiary
-- src:19478 | company of a public interest company, gives notice of
-- src:19479 | resignation under section 205AB(1), and the Registrar
-- src:19484 | approves the resignation of the auditor under
-- src:19485 | section 205AB(2),
-- src:19487 | the directors of the company in question —
-- src:19489 | (c) must call a general meeting of the company as soon as is
-- src:19490 | practicable, and in any case not more than 3 months after
-- src:19491 | the date of the auditor’s resignation, for the purpose of
-- src:19492 | appointing an auditor in place of the auditor who desires to
-- src:19493 | resign or has resigned; and
@ref s 205AF(1)(c) (src:19471-19493)
GIVEN `the date of the auditor's resignation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205AF(1)(c) the last day for the directors to call the general meeting` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the auditor's resignation` 3 Months

@ref s 205AF(1)(c) (src:19471-19493)
GIVEN `the resignation is of a kind that subsection (1)(a) or (b) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the auditor's resignation` IS A DATE
      `the directors have called a general meeting for the purpose of appointing an auditor in place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the directors called the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AF(1)(c) the directors are in default of the duty to call a general meeting` MEANS
    IF     `the resignation is of a kind that subsection (1)(a) or (b) describes`
       AND (NOT `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)`)
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the directors have called a general meeting for the purpose of appointing an auditor in place`
              `the day the directors called the general meeting`
              (`s 205AF(1)(c) the last day for the directors to call the general meeting` `the date of the auditor's resignation`)
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the company in question -- (c) must call a general meeting of the company as soon as is practicable, and in any case not more than 3 months after the date of the auditor's resignation" (a duty met in time, or not yet due, or disapplied by subsection (3): the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 205AF(1)(c) (src:19471-19493)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the date of the auditor's resignation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
`s 205AF(1)(c) the directors must call a general meeting to appoint an auditor in place` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 205AF(1)(c) call a general meeting for the purpose of appointing an auditor in place of the auditor who resigns`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the date of the auditor's resignation` (`s 205AF(1)(c) the last day for the directors to call the general meeting` `the date of the auditor's resignation`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not call a general meeting to appoint an auditor in place within 3 months after the date of the resignation"

-- (1)(d): upon appointment of the new auditor, the directors must lodge with the Registrar a notification of the appointment within 14 days of the appointment.
-- src:19495 | (d) upon appointment of the new auditor, must lodge with the
-- src:19496 | Registrar a notification of such appointment within 14 days
-- src:19497 | of the appointment.
