`s 205AF(1)(d) the last day for the directors to lodge the notification` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the new auditor was appointed` 14 Days

@ref s 205AF(1)(d) (src:19495-19497)
GIVEN `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the new auditor was appointed` IS A DATE
      `the directors have lodged the notification of the appointment with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the directors lodged the notification` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AF(1)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to lodge a notification of the appointment` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)`)
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the directors have lodged the notification of the appointment with the Registrar`
              `the day the directors lodged the notification`
              (`s 205AF(1)(d) the last day for the directors to lodge the notification` `the day the new auditor was appointed`)
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors ... (d) upon appointment of the new auditor, must lodge with the Registrar a notification of such appointment within 14 days of the appointment" (a duty met in time, or not yet due, or disapplied by subsection (3): the provision's own question; fork lines F-D1 and F-P3)

@ref s 205AF(1)(d) (src:19495-19497)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the day the new auditor was appointed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205AA act`
