    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 205AF(1)(d) lodge with the Registrar a notification of the appointment of the new auditor`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the new auditor was appointed` (`s 205AF(1)(d) the last day for the directors to lodge the notification` `the day the new auditor was appointed`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not lodge a notification of the new auditor's appointment within 14 days of the appointment"

-- src:19501 | (2) If the directors of a company fail to appoint an auditor in place
-- src:19502 | of the auditor who desires to resign or has resigned, the Registrar
-- src:19503 | may, on the application in writing of any member of the company,
-- src:19504 | make the appointment.
@ref s 205AF(2) (src:19501-19504)
GIVEN `the directors of the company have failed to appoint an auditor in place of the auditor who desires to resign or has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AF(2) the Registrar may make the appointment on the application of a member` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the company have failed to appoint an auditor in place of the auditor who desires to resign or has resigned` AND `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the directors of a company fail to appoint an auditor in place ..., the Registrar may, on the application in writing of any member of the company, make the appointment" (a "may" whose "if" gate failed: the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

-- (3): subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the financial statements are not required to be audited under the Act, or where the resigning auditor is not the sole auditor.
-- src:19508 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the financial statements
-- src:19509 | of the company are not required to be audited under this Act, or where
-- src:19510 | the resigning auditor is not the sole auditor of the company.
@ref s 205AF(3) (src:19508-19510)
GIVEN `the financial statements of the company are not required to be audited under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resigning auditor is not the sole auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AF(3) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply` MEANS
    IF `the financial statements of the company are not required to be audited under this Act` OR `the resigning auditor is not the sole auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the financial statements of the company are not required to be audited under this Act, or where the resigning auditor is not the sole auditor of the company" (an "if"/"where" gate; a failed gate counts as the text's no: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)

-- src:19514 | (4) An auditor appointed pursuant to subsection (1) or (2) must,
-- src:19515 | unless the auditor is removed or resigns, hold office until the
-- src:19516 | conclusion of the next annual general meeting of the company.
@ref s 205AF(4) (src:19514-19516)
GIVEN `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AF(4) the auditor appointed under subsection (1) or (2) holds office` MEANS
    IF `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, unless the auditor is removed or resigns, hold office until the conclusion of the next annual general meeting of the company" (an "until" bar)
    ELSE (IF `the auditor's office has already ended by removal or resignation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the auditor is removed or resigns" (an "unless" met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:19520 | (5) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the
-- src:19521 | company and every director of the company who is in default shall
-- src:19522 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:19523 | fine not exceeding $5,000.
@ref s 205AF(5) (src:19520-19523)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205AF(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205AF(5) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 205AF(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 205(17) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) any other person` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and every director of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" names the persons it makes guilty (split site (i), fork line F-E1)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1)" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)

@ref s 205AF(5) (src:19520-19523)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205AF(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 205AF(5) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 205AF(5) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with section 205AF(1)` person EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 5000
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty
